WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.760
Show off my 3D printed postcard rack.

00:02.760 --> 00:07.400
This is a postcard holder, purchased used.

00:07.400 --> 00:12.520
Trying to figure out what to do with it, but ended up designing and printing

00:12.520 --> 00:14.900
these 3D printed little carriages. They have drainage holes

00:14.900 --> 00:16.960
that go between, like, below them,

00:16.960 --> 00:18.720
so you can kind of just water at the top, and then the

00:18.720 --> 00:22.100
water goes through and waters the rest of them.

00:22.100 --> 00:24.420
But it makes this amazing display.

00:24.420 --> 00:28.140
I've had it for probably three or four years now, and the plastic is holding up

00:28.140 --> 00:30.420
surprisingly well. It's ABS.

00:30.420 --> 00:34.560
I think it looks beautiful, especially inside in the winter.

00:34.560 --> 00:38.200
I love making use of vertical space, and this has been such a good fit for that.

00:38.200 --> 00:40.540
I'll have the link to the Thingiverse download in there if you want to check that out.
